          %h3#integers Integers
          %h4#inductive_definition Inductive definition
          %p
            Instead of a defining the natural numbers via its induction principle, one can instead define the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            via its induction principle, and then use the fact that disjoint unions are disjoint and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⊎
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \cong \mathbb{Z} \uplus \mathbb{Z}
            to construct the natural numbers.
          %h4#secondorder_definition Second-order definition
          %p
            Alternatively, one can assume a (trichotomous)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+integral+domain"} ordered integral domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/improper+subset"} improper subset
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
            (trichotomous) ordered integral domain and are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+initial+object"} strictly initial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            and a
