                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %p
            In the form of an NNO, the axiom of infinity generalises to the existence of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-type"} W-type
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative
            theories they can be added as additional axioms.
          %p
            One could also posit the existence of the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+natural+numbers"} extended natural numbers
            instead of the set of natural numbers, as the set of extended natural numbers have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable"} countably infinite
            cardinality and is the categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            of the natural numbers in Set, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+coalgebra"} terminal coalgebra
            for the endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) = 1 + X
            in Set. This generalises to the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinductive+types"} coinductive types
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-types"} M-types
          %p
            One could also posit the existence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+finite+types"} type of finite types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            that satisfies the axiom of finiteness (see below).
          %h2#alternatives Alternatives
          %p
            Broadly speaking,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+mathematics"} finite mathematics
            is mathematics that does not use or need the axiom of infinity; a finitist is an extreme breed of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructivist
            that believes that mathematics is better without the axiom of infinity, or even that this axiom is false.
          %p
            A more extreme case is to
            %em deny
            the axiom of infinity with an
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong axiom of finiteness
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            as an axiom of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
          %ul
            %li
              Any property of sets that is invariant under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              and holds for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
              must hold for all sets if, whenever it holds for a set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊎
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \uplus \{*\}
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+foundation"} axiom of foundation
            (which guarantees that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X\}
            are
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+sets"} disjoint
          %ul
            %li
              Any property of sets that holds for the empty set must hold for all sets if, whenever it holds for a set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cup \{X\}
          %p
            In higher categorical terms, the above axiom of finiteness could be stated as follows:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is an initial algebra of the 2-endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \cong X \coprod 1
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
            that is closed under the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
          %ul
            %li
              For all type families
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U \vdash C(A)
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
